# Health data never enters this repository. Verified across all of history on 2026-08-12:
# no tracked database, no SQLite blob among any object in any ref, and no seed file.
#
# The rule is absolute rather than cautious, because the failure is not recoverable. This is a public
# repository, a push is immediately mirrored and indexed, and cycle data identifies pregnancy,
# pregnancy loss and sexual activity. A backfill seed holding one person's real period dates was once
# committed here and had to be purged from history — see docs/HANDOVER.md. Do not relax any line
# below, and do not use `git add -f` to get around one.
#
# `.github/workflows/tests.yml` fails the build if any of these ever appears in a commit, because an
# ignore rule only stops accidents and a forced add is not an accident.

# Databases — the app's own, and anything pulled off a device for debugging.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# The app's exports. Both hold real data: `.cyc` is an encrypted backup, and the clinical summary is
# deliberately plain text so a doctor can read it, which means anyone can.
*.cyc
cycle-summary-*.txt

# Seed / import files. The one that existed held real dates.
seed_*.json
*_periods.json

# Signing credentials. The keystore *is* the app's identity — anyone holding it can publish an
# update that Android will accept as genuine. Losing it is equally bad in the other direction: a
# differently-signed APK cannot be installed over an existing one without uninstalling first, which
# deletes the database. Back both files up outside this repository.
keystore/
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Local environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
local.properties

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
